heptapod@gmail.com wrote:
> I just noticed that brass lanterns are extinguished once someone is
> caught up in a dust vortex.
> 
> All this time I thought that brass lanterns were electrical like the
> ones in Zork especially since you recharge them with a scroll of
> charging not oil.
> 
> Why wouldn't they stay lit other than NHINIRL?

Well, they're primarily dust, but the vortex will pick up just about
anything that masses less than a gram.  With all the thousands of
adventurers who travel to the dungeons to get their possessions
identified the hard way, the dungeon floors are covered in microscopic
iron filings from the impact of weapons on armor.  These get picked up
by the dust vortex along with the dirt, and when an adventurer is
caught up in one, the filings get in the lantern's circuitry and cause
a short.  This then trips the integrated breaker and the lamp turns
off.  You didn't think the DevTeam would overlook this, did you?


